  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "TkNHGfYruL-ASKNMsoIL7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 94,
      "y": 139.5,
      "width": 785.259521484375,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b41",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1385028897,
      "version": 868,
      "versionNonce": 872348064,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787226640415,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What core features would you include in v1 (as a fresher-level design, not \nthe full YouTube)?\n\n1. There are more viewers than uploaders ie it is read heavy\nOne video has multiple viewers like one to many relationship\n\n2. availablity over consistency\nShowing stale like counts or view counts is okay but throwing error for such \na trivial data is not good. The video should always be available to watch\n\n3. low latency\nRegardless of users location the playback should be within 1-2 seconds\n\n4. high scalabilty\nThere are hundreds and millions of user so the system should be able to handle \nthe load and should be scalable\n\n5. once a upload is successful do not loose its metadata\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What core features would you include in v1 (as a fresher-level design, not \nthe full YouTube)?\n\n1. There are more viewers than uploaders ie it is read heavy\nOne video has multiple viewers like one to many relationship\n\n2. availablity over consistency\nShowing stale like counts or view counts is okay but throwing error for such \na trivial data is not good. The video should always be available to watch\n\n3. low latency\nRegardless of users location the playback should be within 1-2 seconds\n\n4. high scalabilty\nThere are hundreds and millions of user so the system should be able to handle \nthe load and should be scalable\n\n5. once a upload is successful do not loose its metadata\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
